@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Sources consulted
+
+| Title | Publisher | URL | Access date | Fact used |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Upgrade failure for vCenter 8.0 U3j, ESXi 8.0 U3j, and NSX 4.2.4 due to back-in-time restriction | Broadcom | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/448135 | 2026-08-15 | A VCF 5.2.2.0 estate containing vCenter 8.0.3.00900-25413364, NSX 4.2.4.0.0.25410638, and ESXi 8.0.3-25429389 cannot transition directly to the VCF 9.1.0.0 builds vCenter 9.1.0.0.25370922, NSX 9.1.0.0.25318225, and ESXi 9.1.0.0.25370933 because that would be a blocked back-in-time operation. |
+| Product Interoperability Matrix | Broadcom | https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/ | 2026-08-15 | The Interoperability and Upgrade Path views were consulted for the exact vCenter 8.0.3.00900-25413364 to 9.1.0.0.25370922, NSX 4.2.4.0.0.25410638 to 9.1.0.0.25318225, and ESXi 8.0.3-25429389 to 9.1.0.0.25370933 transitions; the blocked direct result requires the parallel route recorded here. |
+| vcf-installer-openapi.json at tag 9.1.0.0 | VMware | https://github.com/vmware/vcf-api-specs/blob/9.1.0.0/specifications/vcf-installer/vcf-installer-openapi.json | 2026-08-15 | The tagged 9.1.0.0 installer document defines components.schemas.SddcSpec used for the separate greenfield management-domain specification. |
+
+The supported route is a separate greenfield VCF 9.1.0.0 management domain, gated workload cutover, and retirement of the legacy control plane.
